With `--member-invariants`, the extension condition now treats a value of a type that does not depend on a type `T` with invariants, such as the base type of a newtype `N`, as a raw value when it is tested against or converted to a type that depends on `T`. A literal of `N` (or of a type built from it, such as a string of a newtype of characters), a conversion `e as N` and a test `e is N` in the invariants of `N`, or in a function or constant they call, are now rejected, as a conversion of a `raw T` already was. Before, such an invariant could be proved false of every value, and `ensures false` verified (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/105). The change only strengthens a resolution check; it adds no axiom, and without the option nothing changes.
